## 2026-08-17 — Bootstrap 5.3 CSS-var-only re-theming needs component-level overrides too
Overriding `--bs-primary` and the `-bg-subtle`/`-text-emphasis`/`-rgb` family at `:root` looked complete but wasn't: Bootstrap 5.3's component mixins (`.btn-primary`, form-control focus rings, `.form-check-input:checked`) bake the original `$primary` Sass value into their own local CSS vars at compile time, not `var(--bs-primary)`. Confirmed live in a browser — the login button and every focus ring rendered stock blue despite correct root tokens — not caught by reading the compiled CSS alone. Fixed by overriding each used component's local vars explicitly (see `static/css/theme-overrides.css`'s top comment). Also: Bootstrap's own `.text-bg-*` badge utilities ship with `!important`, so overrides need it too.

## 2026-08-17 — SecurityConfig's CSP blocks all CDN assets by design
CSP is locked to `'self'` everywhere (script/style/font-src) — a deliberate PRD §19.6 decision, not an oversight. A CDN font (Bunny Fonts) was ruled out for exactly this reason. Same-origin webjars are the fix: `org.webjars.npm:<pkg>` on Maven Central mirrors most npm packages, including font packages (`fontsource__inter`) that bundle actual font files with local `@font-face` paths — zero CSP change needed.

## 2026-08-17 — Stale `tenant.primary_color` default caught by grepping the whole repo, not just touched files
Changing the app's theme color in CSS didn't catch two other places the old color lived: an inline-HTML email button (`IdentityEmails.java`) and a DB column default (`tenant.primary_color`, seeded into MHZ's row). Neither showed up searching templates/CSS. Worth a repo-wide grep for the literal old hex value whenever a "the app's color/theme is X" decision changes, not just the files obviously in scope.
